2. On 20-6-1966, the appellants filed the writ petition under Articles 226/227 of the Constitution in the High Court impugning the aforesaid orders of the Collector the Commissioner and the Financial Commissioner, as being illegal and without jurisdiction, inter alia on these grounds:
(i) That no notice as required by Rule 6 of Punjab Security of Land Tenure Rules, 1956 was issued to the appellants; nor were they afforded by the Collector, an opportunity to put forth their objections against the inclusion of the lands purchased by them, in the surplus area;
(ii) That in view of the mandate In
Section 2(5)(2)
of the Act, the lands purchased by the appellants, could not be included in the surplus area of Respondent No. 1, as on the crucial date i.e. 15-4-1953, these lands were in the occupation of tenants whose total holdings did not exceed the permissible limit;
(iii) That the Commissioner erred In himself calling and examining the Khasra Girdawri, and then without even examining the Patwari who had made the entries therein, in holding, on mere conjectures, that the record had been tampered with. Hearing at the appellate stage was no substitute for hearing at the original enquiry.

